Z||000000||87ECO5||06-05-2000||09:07 AM||||OK - I had a problem with a wobbly steering column in my '87 coupe so I pulled it out and installed one from an '84 SE.  Both cars had manual transmission, tilt wheel and delay wipers.  However, the '84 also had cruise control.  So, I removed the cruise/delay wiper stalk from the '84's column and installed the delay wiper stalk from my '87's.<P>Now, I have a little problem to diagnose:  I still have the mist feature (though I now get three swipes of the wipers where I only used to get one - no big deal) and both low and high speeds but the delay portion doesn't work.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-05-2000||09:37 AM||||Try changing the wiper motor.  Maybe that's all that's wrong.  (Of course, this is coming from someone who's afraid to change spark plugs! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||06-05-2000||09:59 AM||||I find it quicker and easier to just fix the wiggle||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||06-05-2000||02:25 PM||||Monkeyman - the wipers worked fine before I changed columns.  I'm wondering if the '87 stalk is not compatible with the '84 column.  I suppose I could put the '84 stalk back onto the column and see if that fixes things.||||reg||1
